# R analysis scripts

Load **`r-human-code`** from this pack when writing or refactoring analysis scripts.

- One script, top to bottom: paths → `library()` block → transform → write
- Workhorse packages: load once, call bare; `pkg::fun()` only for one-offs, masking, or unclear source
- No `source()` helpers, CLI parsing, or one-use custom functions
- No custom functions unless the same chunk repeats and would be verbose inline
- Heavy compute on ANU Dayhoff → separate `.sh` SLURM wrapper (`dayhoff-slurm`)

Do not use generic `r-style-guide`, `tidyverse-patterns`, or `r-tidyverse-style`.
